{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_489123501#0_1051288566","relevance":3,"reason":"The document is dedicated to religious views on euthanasia and explicitly covers Eastern traditions such as Buddhism, Hinduism, Jainism and Shinto alongside Western/Abrahamic traditions such as Christianity, Catholicism, Islam, and Judaism, giving direct evidence on how views vary.","learned":"Buddhist views are not monolithic: compassion may be cited to justify euthanasia by relieving suffering, but many Buddhists still criticize it as intentionally destroying life; the page compares this with multiple other religious traditions."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3211","reason":"This query has found a highly relevant document dedicated to religious views across East and West, so continue for additional segments or similar documents with direct comparative evidence."}}
