{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_489123501#3_1051294734","relevance":3,"reason":"This is a substantive segment of the dedicated 'Religious Views on Euthanasia' page. It directly discusses Western Christian/Catholic and Protestant variation on euthanasia within a broader page that also covers Eastern traditions such as Buddhism, Hinduism, Jainism and Shinto.","learned":"Western Christian views vary: the Roman Catholic Church is unequivocally opposed, Evangelicals often share a sanctity-of-life approach, while some liberal Protestant traditions and clergy have supported limited physician-assisted dying."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3211","reason":"The religious-views query is yielding dedicated comparative evidence, including multiple substantive segments from a directly relevant page; continue to collect additional East/West religious-view evidence."}}
