{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_489123501#8_1051303577","relevance":3,"reason":"This is a substantive segment of the dedicated 'Religious Views on Euthanasia' page. It directly provides Eastern/Jain evidence about sallekhana/santhara, explaining conditions under which fasting unto death is not considered suicide, then transitions to Jewish views, supporting East-West variation in end-of-life ethics.","learned":"Jainism distinguishes sallekhana from suicide when performed under strict conditions, without desire either to live or die; the practice remains controversial in India."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q3211","reason":"The current query has been highly productive and may still contain remaining substantive segments from the dedicated comparative religious-views page, so continue until it is exhausted or starts yielding poor results."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q3211"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_489123501#7_1051301998","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q3211","rank":16,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_28_489123501#7_1051301998\" , \"end_char\": 5670.000000 , \"headings\": \"Religious Views on Euthanasia Religious Views on Euthanasia Page Contents Buddhism Christianity Catholicism Protestantism Christians in support of <cover>euthanasia Hinduism Islam Jainism Judaism Shinto Unitarian Universalism Influence of religious views</cover>See also Adapted from Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia Share this: Like this: Search Quote of the Day \" , \"segment\": \"It is forbidden for a Muslim to plan, or come to know through self-will, the time of his own death in advance. Jainism Main article: Sallekhana Jainism is based on the principle of non-violence ( ahinsa) and is best known for it. Jainism recommends voluntary death or sallekhana for both ascetics and srāvaka (householders) at the end of their life. Sallekhana (also known as Santhara, Samadhi-marana) is made up of two words sal (meaning ‘properly’) and lekhana, which means to thin out. Properly thinning out of the passions and the body is sallekhana. A person is allowed to fast unto death or take the vow of sallekhana only when certain requirements are fulfilled. "}}
